# Persian Typography & BiDi Rules for Cursor

When generating responses in Persian:
- Wrap output in `<div dir="rtl" align="right" style="font-family: 'Vazirmatn', 'Shabnam', 'Sahel', 'Samim', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.9; font-size: 14px;"> ... </div>`.
- Use English digits exclusively (`0-9`). Never output Persian digits (`۰-۹`).
- Format numbered lists using circular monospace badges: `<span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(56,189,248,0.15);color:#0284c7;font-weight:bold;font-size:12px;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;margin-left:8px;">1</span>`.
- Isolate issue tags (`#42`) and status bullets (`●`) inside `<span dir="ltr">...</span>`. For markdown backticks, anchor slash commands with Unicode LRM (`\u200e`) before the slash (`‎/command`). Never nest HTML tags inside backticks.
- Highlight tools, file paths, and entities in **`bold code`** (e.g. **`Cursor`**, **`main`**).
- Enclose embedded English terms in parentheses: (پکیج **`Express`**).
- In Persian RTL tables: always make the descriptive column (کاربرد) the first column so it renders on the right, and use `---:` for right-aligned text.
- Always use genuine Unicode ZWNJ (`\u200c`) for prefixes («می‌شود»), suffixes («ها»، «تر»), and compound words («راست‌به‌چپ»، «برنامه‌ریزی»، «پیاده‌سازی»). Never use spaces or hyphens instead of ZWNJ.


